{The Ghost}
\line
\line
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Description}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {The ghost of Hamlet's father}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Notes}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {The ghost of Hamlet's father who returns to tell his son that he was murdered by Claudius so that Claudius could assume the throne. He wants Hamlet to avenge him. The character is ambiguous\uc1\u8212*Hamlet wonders if the ghost is a demon trying to deceive him\uc1\u8212*and there is no definitive resolution in the play to what causes the ghost to appear.}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Role}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Protagonist's Father}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Motivation}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {To warn his son of the fact that his uncle murdered him, and to challenge him to seek vengence for his death.}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Gender}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Male}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Fatal Flaws}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Too trusting of his brother}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Inner Conflict}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Wants his son to kill his brother to restore his honor}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {How They Die}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {Poisoned in the ear while sleeping in a garden}\par}
{\pard\b\sb100\sa100\fs32\qc {Characters That Die}\b0\par}
{\pard\sb100\sa100 {No}\par}
